  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1100 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nRidging across the central High Plains lead to high temps in the\nlower-80s along and south of I-80 this afternoon and in\nlocalized spots in northeast Nebraska, too. \n\nWind speeds have not fallen off after dark and are expected to\nremain at about 10-20 mph through the night. The southerly flow\nshould help saturate what is currently a pretty dry layer from\nH8 to H7. Deterministic global models and CAMs have been\nconsistently producing isolated light showers along the NE/SD \nstate line overnight thanks to the WAA/moisture advection. Have\nmaintained 15-25% PoPs there from 4am to 9am. The remainder of \nthe area should be dry. A few hundred kJ/g of CAPE means some \nthunder may be heard. The vast majority (or total) of the area\nwill remain dry.",
